      "detail": "10 of the 14 Core1A construction units mount the same horse-and-cart scene (chosen body: cart; F horse-on-cart at θ with F_x, F_y), whatever the unit teaches. For CU-PHY-NLM-IDEAL-STRING-TENSION-1/-2, CU-PHY-NLM-SINGLE-STRING-CONSTRAINT-1/-2 and CU-PHY-NLM-CONNECTED-COMMON-ACCEL-1/-2, no stage shows a string, a pulley, y_A/y_B coordinates, a tension on each body, touching blocks or a system boundary around two bodies. Their worked anchors (cart on a table with a hanging 1 kg mass, a = 10/3 m/s², T = 20/3 N; Atwood 3 kg/1 kg, a = 5 m/s², T = 15 N; blocks 3 kg/2 kg, a = 3 m/s², N = 11 N; buckets, T = 30 N) have nothing drawn. The SECOND-LAW unit's incline step (a_perp = 0, 10 kg on 30°, a = 2 m/s², N ≈ 86.6 N) has no incline. NET-ZERO-MOTION and FORCES-SUM-ZERO show a net pulling force, which is the opposite of the case they teach. Only 3 representations exist in the record; string/pulley, two-block contact and incline representations need to be authored and drawn."
